WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:09.882
"I'm coming, Ello!"

2
00:00:16.445 --> 00:00:17.105
Perda cried.

3
00:00:17.726 --> 00:00:19.086
She dived into the water.

4
00:00:19.987 --> 00:00:22.208
Zann plunged into the chilly sea too.

5
00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:26.649
He dived down into the murky water and spotted Perda just below him.

6
00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:29.771
When he reached her, she had Ello by the arm.

7
00:00:30.911 --> 00:00:34.773
Zann grabbed Ello's other arm and helped Perda drag him back to the surface.

8
00:00:35.354 --> 00:00:37.255
Ello coughed and spit out water.

9
00:00:37.275 --> 00:00:39.357
"Over here!"

10
00:00:39.597 --> 00:00:40.197
Gliss called.

11
00:00:41.038 --> 00:00:43.379
She and Darb reached out to pull Ello aboard.

12
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.221
Then they helped Zann and Perda as well.

13
00:00:46.241 --> 00:00:53.066
"Whew! That was close," Perda said breathlessly.

14
00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:55.288
"What happened?"

15
00:00:55.508 --> 00:00:56.529
Darb asked Ello.

16
00:00:56.949 --> 00:00:57.790
"Can't you swim?"

17
00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:59.831
"Of course I can."

18
00:01:00.211 --> 00:01:01.052
Ello was shaking.

19
00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.181
"I suppose I must be weak from my long solitude.

20
00:01:04.862 --> 00:01:06.462
Let's find a wormhole and get out of here."

21
00:01:06.482 --> 00:01:10.844
"Okay." Zann pulled out the guidelink and handed it to Perda.

22
00:01:10.864 --> 00:01:12.205
"How should we do this?"

23
00:01:13.065 --> 00:01:14.286
Perda rubbed the device.

24
00:01:14.306 --> 00:01:17.487
"Think about wormholes, everyone," she said.

25
00:01:17.507 --> 00:01:19.128
"Or the vortex.

26
00:01:19.708 --> 00:01:20.608
Either one might work."

27
00:01:21.369 --> 00:01:23.310
Several gulpers surfaced nearby.

28
00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:25.951
Then there was a tug on the guidelink.

29
00:01:27.231 --> 00:01:28.352
"This way," Perda said.

30
00:01:29.024 --> 00:01:31.806
She held on tightly as the device pulled the boat along.

31
00:01:32.487 --> 00:01:33.488
The gulpers followed.

32
00:01:34.989 --> 00:01:36.430
Darb eyed the gulpers.

33
00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:40.454
"I hope the guidelink helps us get to the wormhole first.

34
00:01:41.174 --> 00:01:44.097
Otherwise all it's doing is helping those things find a snack."

35
00:01:45.057 --> 00:01:48.560
"Maybe we should all hold the guidelink," Gliss suggested.

36
00:01:49.321 --> 00:01:50.922
Everyone put a hand on the device.

37
00:01:51.703 --> 00:01:53.344
Zann glanced at Ello's hand.

38
00:01:53.364 --> 00:01:57.608
"Ello, it might work better if you take off your gloves," he said.

39
00:01:58.368 --> 00:02:01.290
Before Ello could respond, the boat rocketed forward.

40
00:02:02.231 --> 00:02:04.252
The guidelink vibrated under their hands.

41
00:02:05.053 --> 00:02:07.034
The gulpers were soon far behind.

42
00:02:07.054 --> 00:02:09.136
Perda pointed ahead.

43
00:02:09.156 --> 00:02:10.577
"There's a wormhole!"

44
00:02:11.518 --> 00:02:12.198
Zann nodded.

45
00:02:12.218 --> 00:02:14.160
"Get ready to jump, everyone!"

46
00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:16.141
"What about the boat?"

47
00:02:16.321 --> 00:02:16.822
Darb said.

48
00:02:16.842 --> 00:02:18.763
"We'll have to leave it behind."

49
00:02:19.724 --> 00:02:23.326
Zann glanced over his shoulder and saw that the gulpers were gaining on them.

50
00:02:23.346 --> 00:02:25.488
"There's no time to deflate it."

51
00:02:26.368 --> 00:02:28.230
Darb nodded, but he looked uneasy.

52
00:02:29.151 --> 00:02:30.732
Perda performed a Shackle spell.

53
00:02:31.553 --> 00:02:35.796
With everyone shackled together, Zann got ready for the leap into the wormhole.

54
00:02:36.617 --> 00:02:37.938
"Now!" Zann cried.

55
00:02:38.779 --> 00:02:39.620
Everyone jumped.

56
00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:46.246
Whoosh! A moment later they were spinning through the vortex again.

57
00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.727
"We did it!"

58
00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:48.788
Gliss exclaimed.

59
00:02:48.808 --> 00:02:52.992
"I've never been so happy to be in this crazy place."

60
00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:54.941
Perda laughed.

61
00:02:55.861 --> 00:02:57.763
"I know what you mean."

62
00:02:58.583 --> 00:03:01.786
She glanced at Ello, who was shackled between her and Zann.

63
00:03:01.806 --> 00:03:04.768
"Welcome to the vortex, Ello."

64
00:03:04.788 --> 00:03:07.510
"What?" Ello looked around.

65
00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.291
"Oh, right.

66
00:03:09.792 --> 00:03:11.613
This is my first time in the vortex."

67
00:03:11.633 --> 00:03:14.195
"That's weird," Zann thought.

68
00:03:14.975 --> 00:03:16.957
Ello sounded flat and unimpressed.

69
00:03:17.998 --> 00:03:21.020
Usually people were freaked out during their first time in the vortex.

70
00:03:22.312 --> 00:03:24.574
"Let's see if we can find your people," Zann said.

71
00:03:24.594 --> 00:03:28.277
"Did Wyssa tell you anything about the world where she was bringing them?

72
00:03:29.098 --> 00:03:33.362
If we know what type of magic it has, maybe we can use the guidelink to find it."

73
00:03:33.382 --> 00:03:36.405
"I have no idea," Ello said.

74
00:03:36.425 --> 00:03:38.607
"Wyssa didn't tell us anything.

75
00:03:40.208 --> 00:03:42.210
Maybe I should just come back to Magica with you.

76
00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:43.671
I've always wanted to visit."

77
00:03:44.732 --> 00:03:46.293
Gliss raised an eyebrow.

78
00:03:46.313 --> 00:03:49.136
"Don't you want to find your family?"

79
00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:54.801
"I'm sure you know some powerful people in Magica who can help me get home," Ello said.

80
00:03:55.741 --> 00:03:56.842
Zann was surprised.

81
00:03:57.762 --> 00:04:02.803
When his parents were lost in the vortex, Zann wanted more than anything to be reunited with them.

82
00:04:03.564 --> 00:04:06.744
But Ello didn't seem to be in much of a hurry to find his own family.

83
00:04:07.885 --> 00:04:10.065
Perda gave Ello a suspicious look.

84
00:04:10.545 --> 00:04:13.986
"Why wouldn't Wyssa tell your people where she was taking them?"

85
00:04:14.006 --> 00:04:19.968
"She might have been distracted by Morb," Gliss suggested before Ello could respond.

86
00:04:20.788 --> 00:04:23.669
"Maybe she was still trying to figure out what to do with Morb."

87
00:04:23.689 --> 00:04:25.050
"That's it!"

88
00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:26.110
Ello said quickly.

89
00:04:26.751 --> 00:04:27.891
"She did seem distracted.

90
00:04:28.171 --> 00:04:29.452
And Morb kept trying to escape.

91
00:04:30.132 --> 00:04:31.973
That's probably why she didn't tell us anything."

92
00:04:31.993 --> 00:04:34.874
"She brought Morb with her to Skellia?"

93
00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.454
Zann was surprised again.

94
00:04:36.474 --> 00:04:38.135
"Why would she do that?"

95
00:04:38.155 --> 00:04:41.436
"And didn't your people ask any questions?"

96
00:04:41.677 --> 00:04:42.517
Perda persisted.

97
00:04:42.537 --> 00:04:45.738
"Your mother or Rellu weren't curious?"

98
00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:47.859
"Who?" Ello said.

99
00:04:48.619 --> 00:04:49.760
Zann stared at him.

100
00:04:50.692 --> 00:04:51.873
"Rellu," he repeated.

101
00:04:51.893 --> 00:04:53.913
"The elder from your village."

102
00:04:53.933 --> 00:04:56.054
"Oh, him."

103
00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:57.475
Ello cleared his throat.

104
00:04:57.495 --> 00:04:59.176
"Of course.

105
00:04:59.636 --> 00:05:00.996
I, uh, didn't hear you."

106
00:05:01.957 --> 00:05:04.618
Zann couldn't ignore his uneasy feelings anymore.

107
00:05:05.478 --> 00:05:07.239
Something about Ello was odd.

108
00:05:07.799 --> 00:05:11.901
And judging by the suspicious look on her face, Perda felt the same way.

109
00:05:12.962 --> 00:05:14.902
Perda gestured to an approaching wormhole.

110
00:05:14.922 --> 00:05:16.083
"Let's exit here.

111
00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:18.484
I think we need to have a talk."

112
00:05:19.208 --> 00:05:24.471
Zann grabbed the edge of the wormhole, peeking through to make sure it didn't look like Fardark or

113
00:05:24.591 --> 00:05:25.932
any other unpleasant world.

114
00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:31.175
The landscape was covered in ice and snow, but otherwise didn't seem dangerous.

115
00:05:33.476 --> 00:05:37.058
When they'd landed in the soft snow, Perda dissolved the shackles.

116
00:05:37.078 --> 00:05:39.719
"Brr!" Gliss said.

117
00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:43.101
She snapped her fingers to conjure a warm coat.

118
00:05:43.121 --> 00:05:46.223
"Hey, our magic seems to work here."

119
00:05:47.083 --> 00:05:49.232
Perda was staring at Ello.

120
00:05:49.252 --> 00:05:52.753
"So, Ello, tell us again exactly how you got left behind."

121
00:05:52.773 --> 00:05:56.474
"And where that houseboat came from," Zann added.

122
00:05:57.274 --> 00:05:58.074
Ello frowned.

123
00:05:58.094 --> 00:05:59.935
"Why are you interrogating me?"

124
00:06:00.175 --> 00:06:00.695
he whined.

125
00:06:00.715 --> 00:06:04.116
"I just want to get back to the safety of Magica."

126
00:06:04.136 --> 00:06:08.477
"But you've never even been to Magica," Perda said.

127
00:06:08.497 --> 00:06:11.498
"Why don't you want to find your family instead?"

128
00:06:11.518 --> 00:06:13.499
"Yeah," Gliss said.

129
00:06:13.519 --> 00:06:15.399
"That does seem weird."

130
00:06:16.099 --> 00:06:17.000
Ello scowled.

131
00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.300
"Fine," he said.

132
00:06:19.008 --> 00:06:19.829
"You want answers?

133
00:06:20.009 --> 00:06:20.690
Here you go!"

134
00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:21.991
He snapped his fingers.

135
00:06:22.971 --> 00:06:25.674
Ello's familiar face began to change appearance.

136
00:06:26.474 --> 00:06:28.096
Zann watched with confusion.

137
00:06:29.036 --> 00:06:30.518
Then he gasped.

138
00:06:31.298 --> 00:06:32.439
Ello's face was gone.

139
00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:37.043
In its place was a different, even more familiar one.

140
00:06:38.024 --> 00:06:39.545
"Morb!" Zann cried.

141
00:06:40.245 --> 00:06:41.487
Perda's eyes widened.

142
00:06:41.507 --> 00:06:43.929
"You used a Masking spell!"

143
00:06:44.689 --> 00:06:45.890
"Clever girl."

144
00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:47.812
Morb glared at the kids.

145
00:06:48.636 --> 00:06:53.201
"All of you really are too clever for your own good."

146
00:06:53.241 --> 00:06:57.146
Before the kids could react, he plucked the guidelink out of Perda's hand.

147
00:06:58.026 --> 00:07:02.892
With a triumphant cackle, he disappeared through the wormhole.
